{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/944976-protection-against-blood-bound","id":944976,"title":"Protection against blood bound","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-06T11:49:25-07:00","id":944976,"title":"Protection against blood bound","content":"Hi guys, need some help<br /> <br /> In the book blood sorcery you can use protection 4 to defend yourself when drink vitae from another vampire. Yu guys think if it\u00b4s possible reduce some blood bound in progress? (not a permanent one, but 2 or 1 steps)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12224-montoya","name":"Montoya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T15:32:50-07:00","id":945098,"title":"","content":"The blood bond isn't mind-control and can be negated by refusing Vitae for roughly one year. So yes, you can reduce the blood bond.<br /> <br /> As a PC, if they are aware of the BB and its nature, they could hit up the self-help section of the book store for an equipment bonus to counter any pressure your would-be dominator puts on you, and for ways to control any blood addiction you might have. If you can't resist them at all, you could go nuclear and intentionally bond yourself to a safer bet, ending any two or one stage bond in infancy. So two options without the introduction of special powers. Beyond that, go talk to the Ordo. They might be willing to help for a price.<br /> <br /> Note: I might be misreading. If you are asking if 'Protection 4', which I'm unfamiliar with but that you claim protects you when you drink Vitae, could be used to break stage one and two BB, then my reply is that the game is a toolbox and homebrew accepting. In the case of ambiguity, rule in a way that is interesting and fun for the table. In the case of expansion, I don't see how homebrewing an accelerator would break the game given it can be broke naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T02:12:54-07:00","id":945367,"title":"","content":"I've always seen the lists within Blood Sorcery's theme levels were more examples than complete acknowledgement of all possibilities. So, I'd say getting rid of it AFTER the fact would probably be Protection 5, a level higher, as it seems fitting. Protection 4 might give you a dice bonus to help make the rolls needed to act against the Domitor, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T07:52:42-07:00","id":945457,"title":"","content":"I think it's a lot harder to get rid of something once you have it... I dont think Protection 5 would allow it. I think that since it says &quot;unreliable myths&quot; You are looking at homebrew stuff to get rid of it once you have caught it. I think of Protection as protection against something that would happen or could happen, but once it's happened.. there arent many ways to protect yourself against it anymore. Perhaps like a cliche salt circle... but once they are in it.. you cant just draw a better one.. because they are still in it...<br /> <br /> &quot;Outside waiting out the year, methods for diffusing the bond \u2014 save<br /> for an overwhelming third-stage bond \u2014 are unreliable myths<br /> at best.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I dont think that the blood bond is necessarily something you know you have either. ( I am not saying there isnt a situation out there where you do know, as there are. ) but remember in usual circumstances it takes time and feelings are fluid, you could have changed your feelings naturally. <br /> <br /> That said.. If you were totally in love with someone, getting rid of that bond might hurt them ( breaking point. ) so, why would you want to do that to someone you care so much about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-07-2016, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T08:17:46-07:00","id":945468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/944976-protection-against-blood-bound?p=945457#post945457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a lot harder to get rid of something once you have it... I dont think Protection 5 would allow it. I think that since it says &quot;unreliable myths&quot; You are looking at homebrew stuff to get rid of it once you have caught it. I think of Protection as protection against something that would happen or could happen, but once it's happened.. there arent many ways to protect yourself against it anymore. Perhaps like a cliche salt circle... but once they are in it.. you cant just draw a better one.. because they are still in it...<br /> <br /> &quot;Outside waiting out the year, methods for diffusing the bond \u2014 save<br /> for an overwhelming third-stage bond \u2014 are unreliable myths<br /> at best.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I dont think that the blood bond is necessarily something you know you have either. ( I am not saying there isnt a situation out there where you do know, as there are. ) but remember in usual circumstances it takes time and feelings are fluid, you could have changed your feelings naturally.<br /> <br /> That said.. If you were totally in love with someone, getting rid of that bond might hurt them ( breaking point. ) so, why would you want to do that to someone you care so much about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering there's a 2 dot Threnody that can do it, I don't think allowing blood magic to do it is all that big a deal (especially if it's just 1-2 drinks, not a complete Bond). Granted, that Threnody's way too powerful for what it is. Regardless, Protection can heal wounds too, so it's not like it's ONLY prevention. That said, though, I could see maybe also needing to add on some Transmutation, to help bring the person back to a 'normal' state.<br /> <br /> As for if you'd actually do it, well, that's an RP concern and depends on the game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T08:43:44-07:00","id":945479,"title":"","content":"Yes, the bond is not complete (2 steps). And the idea of using transmutation is excellent. For the record, the person who is seeking the &quot;cure&quot; is not the person who drink the blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12224-montoya","name":"Montoya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T13:30:05-07:00","id":945631,"title":"","content":"In 2e there's a Cruac ritual that keeps you from developing blood bonds but explicitly can't cure existing ones. There is a scale of the dragon that lets you waterboard the blood bond out of other people, but probably not yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}